    "body": "closes #40588\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n`:Man` used to keep rendered `man://` buffers loaded after their windows were closed because they can take a while to load. a4c4b39d55 switched man buffers from `bufhidden=hide` to `bufhidden=unload` to fix stale wrapping man width stuff... apprently. this (unintentionally?) reverted the caching.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nKeep regular `:Man` buffers hidden and loaded. Prevent regressoin by storing the effective `MANWIDTH` used to render them; **refresh only if the width has changed.** This is not perfect but a decent compromise IMO.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-06T10:45:11Z",
